# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b2), edited. morgan's first conversation.

~ start
set morgan_met
Narrator: Dried yarrow and bog-mint brush your shoulders as vials clink on crooked shelves. Morgan looks up with faraway green eyes and root-stained violet fingers.
morgan [smile]: Come in, mind the low beam. I was just labelling the willow-water, unless I finished that an hour ago.
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask about their remedies and work -> about_self
* Ask how long they have lived in Wickermoor -> about_village
* Ask about the stranger vials on the back shelf -> rumour
* [Medicine DC 13] Notice the gaps in their ledger notes -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ menu
morgan [neutral]: Was there another draught you needed, or did we only just begin talking?
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask about their remedies and work -> about_self
* Ask how long they have lived in Wickermoor -> about_village
* Ask about the stranger vials on the back shelf -> rumour
* [Medicine DC 13] Notice the gaps in their ledger notes -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
morgan [smile]: Red bottles mend torn flesh, and herb bundles comfort the locals, though comfort does half the curing.
shop
-> menu

~ about_self
morgan [neutral]: I only have bottles and poultices to carry home. People tell me their aches, and I try to remember which jar eased them last time.
-> menu

~ about_village
morgan [weary]: Everyone in the hollow has an old name and an older grave to tend. I wonder what name I had before the moor took me in.
-> menu

~ rumour
morgan [sly]: Some nights I brew tinctures to see through mist or hear the dead whisper in the thatch. I never recall who taught me the measure.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: The open ledger on the counter has pages torn short, ink trails stopping mid-word as if the hand froze.
morgan [sad]: The clock strikes one bell, I blink, and it strikes the next. I woke here small and alone, and the years still slip through my fingers.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
Narrator: Morgan gently closes the stained ledger under a bundle of dried chamomile.
morgan [smile]: Do not mind my messy handwriting, nobody in the hollow can read apothecary scrawl anyway.
-> menu
